---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---
<BaseLayout title="Privacy | The Royal House of Engagement" description="How Low Value Content handles information on the Royal House of Engagement website and in shop orders.">
  <article class="plain-page">
    <header><p class="eyebrow">Draft · November 23, 2026</p><h1>Privacy.</h1><p>We collect only what we need to take payment and ship your shirt. There are no customer accounts, advertising pixels, or behavioral analytics.</p></header>
    <div class="rows">
    <section><h2>Information collected</h2><p>Browsing the site: our hosting provider processes ordinary technical request information, such as IP address, browser, page and time, to deliver and secure the site. Ordering: your name, email, shipping address and order contents. Payment details are entered with Stripe and never reach our servers.</p></section><section><h2>How we use it</h2><p>To process payment and tax, print and ship your order, send order updates, and answer support requests. We do not sell your information.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Restricted environments</h2><p>Development and staging versions use Google and Firebase authentication. An authorized email address may be retained in session storage for the current browser session. This access gate is not used on the public production site.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Who receives it</h2><p>Stripe (payment and tax calculation), Printify and its print providers (production and shipping, which need your name and address), and Google Firebase (our hosting and order records). Each handles data under its own privacy terms. We may disclose information if the law requires it.</p></section><section><h2>Retention</h2><p>We keep order records as long as needed for tax, accounting, and support, then delete them.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Your choices</h2><p>To ask for a copy of your information or its deletion, write to us. We will help unless the law requires us to keep a record. If we add email lists or analytics, we will update this notice first.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Contact</h2><p><a href="mailto:support@lowvaluecontent.com">support@lowvaluecontent.com</a></p></section>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
